# Rotate touchscreen input to match the kiosk display rotation.
#
# When the kiosk is rotated via wlr-randr (KIOSK_ROTATE=90), the display
# pipeline shows everything rotated 90° CW but libinput is still reporting
# touch coordinates in the panel's native (landscape) frame. The result is
# that a finger tap registers somewhere completely different than expected.
#
# This rule applies a 2x3 affine transformation matrix to every touchscreen
# at the libinput layer, before cage / Chromium ever see the event. The
# values below correspond to the rotation directions used elsewhere in this
# project; the installer picks the matching one based on $KIOSK_ROTATE.
#
# 90° CW    →  0 -1 1   1  0 0
# 180°      → -1  0 1   0 -1 1
# 270° CW   →  0  1 0  -1  0 1
# normal    →  1  0 0   0  1 0
#
# The installer writes the active matrix to /etc/udev/rules.d/. We keep the
# template here so it's versioned along with the rest of the kiosk config.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}=="1", \
  ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="__MATRIX__"
